                        "source_sense_id": "ff2cdc66-d317-381f-9df6-47a4da851652",
                        "source_sense_description": "een wapen met vier of meer punten waarvan er altijd een naar boven staat",
                        "target_lang_word": "caltrop",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caltrop",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e0bb0c4-1db6-34c0-8d93-6ec74c96f33a",
                                        "entry_id": "94b134e2-9740-3a47-9e42-4cad64ca1315",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metal object, usually small, with spikes arranged so that, when thrown onto the ground, one always faces up as a threat to pedestrians, horses, and vehicles (also used as a heraldic charge)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "424272f9-7934-42f2-9373-301395f08472",
                                                "sense_id": "4e0bb0c4-1db6-34c0-8d93-6ec74c96f33a",
                                                "text": "[…] her father, the emperor Alexius, who reigned AD 1081-1118, ordered caltrops to be cast in front of his archers […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6d85602-4922-4149-92f2-7634769e48db",
                                                "sense_id": "4e0bb0c4-1db6-34c0-8d93-6ec74c96f33a",
                                                "text": "By Sung times, several different types of caltrops had been developed. As in earlier times, both caltrops could be made from both wood and iron..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d65a6c4-4be7-4ebb-b66c-a3e3dd40e3d9",
                                                "sense_id": "4e0bb0c4-1db6-34c0-8d93-6ec74c96f33a",
                                                "text": "Caltrops, tetrahedrons, and similar devices are designed to puncture vehicle tires or limit foot traffic. The standard design has four points."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7cb4458-fc2b-3af2-b559-d8abe274eca3",
                                        "entry_id": "94b134e2-9740-3a47-9e42-4cad64ca1315",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The starthistle, Centaurea calcitrapa, a plant with sharp thorns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37669add-e634-3806-81fc-5b6f44391a4c",
                                        "entry_id": "94b134e2-9740-3a47-9e42-4cad64ca1315",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a number of flowering plants in the family Zygophyllaceae, including several members of the genus Kallstroemia and the species Tribulus terrestris, native to warm temperate and tropical regions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7ab453db-46e3-43b0-9c77-16f844201596",
                        "source_entry_id": "9fd13aae-703b-3d1c-b907-4081e33d42b1",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff2cdc66-d317-381f-9df6-47a4da851652",
                        "source_sense_description": "een wapen met vier of meer punten waarvan er altijd een naar boven staat",
                        "target_lang_word": "mantrap",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mantrap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d319f44-b776-3d51-ae55-c436514c7391",
                                        "entry_id": "c62877b1-e040-31c8-9ff3-b35b11b47837",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mechanical device for catching trespassers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61ef7ebf-4340-4d16-95a2-7451ca7565fc",
                                                "sense_id": "0d319f44-b776-3d51-ae55-c436514c7391",
                                                "text": "The space had been cleared of landmines and mantraps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80779d56-6ed2-37c3-8d40-ac61cf4c832b",
                                        "entry_id": "c62877b1-e040-31c8-9ff3-b35b11b47837",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small space with two sets of interlocking doors, such that the first set of doors must close before the second set opens, used to restrict access."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcb2c519-4bfe-32c7-a97c-0f386a03eb80",
                                        "entry_id": "c62877b1-e040-31c8-9ff3-b35b11b47837",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woman who is dangerously seductive to men."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09e4a3d2-9662-4019-918c-3c0e76db45bc",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb2c519-4bfe-32c7-a97c-0f386a03eb80",
                                                "text": "\"Don't know the manners of good society, eh? Wal, I guess I know enough to turn you inside out, old gal — you sockdologizing old man-trap.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffb8ea8a-cef8-4000-98b8-944eedd96b65",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb2c519-4bfe-32c7-a97c-0f386a03eb80",
                                                "text": "If anything, she was worse since she had enough money to implement her desires. They were merely in the trade for business reasons. No—Eloise would be something to steer clear of. Alexander was right. She was a mantrap."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
